## What Problem This Solves

Fixes #205881: a provider overload returned by an isolated cron run was recorded as `unknown`, suppressing its transient retry.

Fixes #205881

## Why This Change Was Made

The finalization error path now uses the existing `resolveCronRunErrorReason` provider classifier, matching the thrown-error path. This preserves explicit terminal outcomes and the current unknown fallback.

## User Impact

Scheduled jobs retry transient provider overloads promptly instead of waiting for the next natural schedule.

## Evidence

- The same `runCronIsolatedAgentTurn` boundary yields `unknown`/no retry on pinned base `fbd85e4cdc3f8ba088bac086679091ac630a27e8` and `overloaded`/30-second retry on head `56fc1d704607eab70b2eaf91b7461924a7bd12ae`; the `auth_permanent` control remains non-retryable.

```text
$ OPENCLAW_CRON_RETURNED_ERROR_PROOF=1 pnpm test src/cron/isolated-agent/run.terminal-error-identity.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 -t 'classifies and persists'
base: {"errorClassification":{"kind":"reason","reason":"unknown"},"retryDecision":{"retryable":false,"reason":"permanent error"}}
head: {"errorClassification":{"kind":"reason","reason":"overloaded"},"retryDecision":{"retryable":true,"retryCategory":"overloaded","backoffMs":30000,"reason":"transient retry"}}
negative control: {"permanentControl":{"retryable":false,"reason":"permanent error"}}
